{"content":[{"c":["NICANOR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. The son of Patroclus, “one of the king’s chief friends” (",{"href":"?bref=2Macc.8.9","r":"2Macc.8.9","rawR":"2Macc.8.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Macc.8.9","value":"2Macc.8.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Macc 8:9"},") and a Syrian general under Antiochus IV Epiphanes and Demetrius Soter. This general may have been the supreme commander over Ptolemy and Gorgias in Lysias’s first campaign against Judas Maccabeus (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.3.38-59","r":"1Macc.3.38-59","rawR":"1Macc.3.38-59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.3.38-59","value":"1Macc.3.38-59"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 3:38ff"},".) during the reign of Antiochus IV Epiphanes. He was slain in the battle at Adasa and Beth-horon (161 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). According to 2 Maccabees, Judas hung Nicanor’s head from the citadel as a clear proof of the Lord’s victory (",{"href":"?bref=2Macc.15.35","r":"2Macc.15.35","rawR":"2Macc.15.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Macc.15.35","value":"2Macc.15.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the seven chosen by the early church to supervise the daily distribution to the poor saints in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.6.5","r":"Acts.6.5","rawR":"Acts.6.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.6.5","value":"Acts.6.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 6:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Nicanor","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Macc 8:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Macc.8.9","rawQueryValue":"2Macc.8.9","sourceRefExact":"2Macc.8.9"},{"anchorText":"1 Macc 3:38ff","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.3.38-59","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.3.38-59","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.3.38-59"},{"anchorText":"15:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Macc.15.35","rawQueryValue":"2Macc.15.35","sourceRefExact":"2Macc.15.35"},{"anchorText":"Acts 6:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.6.5","rawQueryValue":"Acts.6.5","sourceRefExact":"Acts.6.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4e3077bda676eb675f22037713c5d0945e9a3f74fc77cab95f2431859669810c","sourceItemName":"Nicanor","sourceItemOrder":137,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Nicanor","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Nicanor","title":"Nicanor","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}